3 1 New Section; Advisory Committee on State Procurement of Agricultural Products. Amend
4 RSA21-Ibyinsertingaftersection14-dthefollowingnewsection:
5 21-I:14-e AdvisoryCommitteeonStateProcurementofAgriculturalProducts.
6 I. Thereisestablishedanadvisorycommitteeonstateprocurementofagriculturalproducts.
7 II. The members of the committee shall be 3 members of the house of representatives,
8 appointed by the speaker of the house of representatives and one senate member appointed by the
9 president.
10 III. Thecommitteeshall:
11 (a) Assesscurrentpracticesforprocuringlocallyproducedfood.
12 (b) Evaluate economic and environmental impacts of supporting conservation-focused
13 farming.
14 (c) Developrecommendationsforpotentialincentivemechanisms.
15 (d) Alignfindingswithstatefoodsystemplanninggoals.
16 IV. The members of the committee shall elect a chairperson from among the members. The
17 firstmeetingofthecommitteeshallbecalledbythefirst-namedhousemember. Thefirstmeetingof
18 the committee shall be held within 45 days of the effective date of this section. Two members of the
19 committeeshallconstituteaquorum.
20 V. BeginningNovember1,2025andeachNovember1thereafter,thecommitteeshallreport
21 its findings and any recommendations for proposed legislation to the speaker of the house of
22 representatives,thepresidentofthesenate,thehouseclerks,thesenateclerk,thegovernor,andthe
23 chairoftheadvisorycommitteeonstateprocurementestablishedinRSA21-I:14-d.
24 2 EffectiveDate. Thisactshalltakeeffectuponitspassage.
